error[NK1164]: `Obj::read[i64]` needs a `Struct` here, but `i64` isn't one.
   --> tests/grammar_a_rule_bound_is_checked.nika:10:15
    |
 10 | 	let n: i64 = Obj::read[i64](Bytes("42".bytes().collect())) catch {
    |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `[S: Struct]` asks what a type is, not what it does, so it's answered by the declaration, not an `impl`. `i64` is a built-in type, which is neither.
    = help: Pass a type declared with `struct`, or remove the bound.
